From: At30c <173511395+At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m21s: prepare TEEgris IWD device nodes

The TEEgris client library creates its probe socket through /dev/tziwsock,
not /dev/tzdev.  Normal boot reports EACCES from iwd_socket while the legacy
device nodes can remain root:root 0600 when their vendor ueventd rules are not
re-applied by the newer init stack.

Restore the vendor labels and enforce the original F415F ownership/modes for
all three TEEgris nodes before starting its daemons.  Keep tziwshmem at 0660,
matching the stock vendor rule.

--- a/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
+++ b/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
@@ -6,6 +6,12 @@ on post-fs
     restorecon /dev/tzdev
     chown system system /dev/tzdev
     chmod 0666 /dev/tzdev
+    restorecon /dev/tziwsock
+    chown system system /dev/tziwsock
+    chmod 0666 /dev/tziwsock
+    restorecon /dev/tziwshmem
+    chown system system /dev/tziwshmem
+    chmod 0660 /dev/tziwshmem
     start tz_service
     start tz_msg_recv
 
